  "description": "OQENIK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C172 H168 N6 Nd14 O80. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd8 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd9 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd10 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd11 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd12 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd13 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd14 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.635-3.783 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.71-104.66°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd14L20(OAc)2(DMF)6(MeOH)10]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
